course: dictionary
lesson: 10700
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues around the word show you which meaning the writer means. «Jobs at unsocial hours, like nights and weekends, often pay more per hour because fewer people want those hours.» The clue is hours, so unsocial here describes when people work, not how someone behaves.
explain: The first meaning is about people. Unsocial means not wanting to be with other people, or not friendly in company. If someone «stays in his room and never joins in», you might call him unsocial. Test it: put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Unsociable is close to unsocial in this sense. Be careful with antisocial, though: it is different and means harmful to others. Do not mix these two words up.
fact: Unsocial has two meanings: not friendly or not wanting company, and, in the UK, Ireland and Australia, working at night, early in the morning or at weekends.
fact: Unsocial hours are working hours when most people are not at work, such as nights and weekends.
fact: Nurses, police and bakers often work unsocial hours, and this work can pay extra.
fact: «Unsocial hours» often pay more per hour, as the example sentence shows, because fewer people want those hours.
fact: Antisocial is different from unsocial: it means harmful to others.
exercise: «Jobs at unsocial hours, like nights and weekends, often pay more per hour.» What are unsocial hours? | Hours spent asleep in bed | Hours spent talking to friends | *Working hours at night, early in the morning or at weekends | Hours when everyone is at school
exercise: Mia says, «Sam is unsocial; he never joins in or talks to anyone at the party.» What does unsocial mean here? | Very loud and noisy | *Not wanting to be with other people | Harmful to others | Working late at night
exercise: Which word means harmful to others? | *Antisocial | Unsocial | Unsociable | Social
test: In the sentence «Jobs at unsocial hours often pay more per hour because fewer people want those hours», what is the reason given? | Nobody works at night | *Fewer people want those hours | The hours are short | Bakers are very rich
test: Which meaning fits «an unsocial neighbour who never says hello»? | Giving out light | Very old | Working at weekends | *Not friendly and not wanting company
exam: Which word describes working at nights and weekends, when most people are not at work? | Social | Friendly | *Unsocial | Antisocial
